# Architecture Rules

- Modular monolith: business capabilities behind explicit app/domain boundaries, not premature service splits.
- Target capability sequence: authentication → business profile → capability registry → policy/context → runtime/workflow → approvals/audit → control tower → AI agent integration → E2E qualification.
- Code owns the workflow; TypeSafe System One only annotates (confidence thresholds: act >= 0.70, escalate < 0.40).
- TypeSafe client closes in FastAPI `lifespan` shutdown.
- Alembic single head (`0007_operation_orchestration`); migrations are reversible where possible.
- Idempotency: fingerprint-verified; legacy rows without fingerprint → `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED` conflict.
- Cross-module orchestration: 6-state lifecycle (PENDING/PROCESSING/COMMITTED/FAILED/RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED/CANCELLED).
